# modules/scan/env.schema — KEY=description:required|optional
#
# scan is DEFAULT OFF. These two keys are not generated by the installer's
# secret bootstrap, because a firm that never enables scan should never carry
# them. Before selecting the scan module, add both to /etc/vibe-sentinel/.env:
#
#   GREENBONE_DB_PASSWORD=$(openssl rand -hex 24)
#   GREENBONE_ADMIN_PASSWORD=$(openssl rand -base64 18)
#
# The installer's env.schema validation refuses to build the stack until they
# are present, with the key name in the message.
GREENBONE_DB_PASSWORD=Password for Greenbone's own Postgres (gb-pg), separate from the shared Sentinel instance:required
GREENBONE_ADMIN_PASSWORD=Initial Greenbone admin password for the loopback web UI on 127.0.0.1:9392:required
GREENBONE_SCAN_TARGETS=Comma-separated CIDRs the scheduled authenticated scans cover, reached over the mesh:optional
GREENBONE_SCAN_SCHEDULE=Cron expression for the scheduled scan; defaults to the firm maintenance window:optional
TZ=Firm timezone; scan schedules and report timestamps render in it:optional
